{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["<b>All the days of its desolation.</b> A term of being made desolate, and the mem has a dagesh in place of the doubled שְׁמָמָה." "<b>That which it did not rest.</b> The seventy years of the Babylonian exile corresponded to the seventy years of shemittah and jubilee that fell during the years when Israel provoked in their land before the Omnipresent — four hundred and thirty years; three hundred and ninety were the years of their iniquity from when they entered the land until the ten tribes were exiled, and the children of Judah provoked Him for forty years from when the ten tribes were exiled until the destruction of Jerusalem. As it says in Ezekiel: ״וְאַתָּה שְׁכַב עַל צִדְּךָ הַשְּׂמָאלִי וְגוֹ׳, וְכִלִּיתָ אֶת אֵלֶּה וְגוֹ׳, וְשָׁכַבְתָּ עַל צִדְּךָ הַיְמָנִי אַרְבָּעִים יוֹם וְנָשָׂאתָ אֶת עֲוֹן בֵּית יְהוּדָה״. And this prophecy was spoken to Ezekiel in the fifth year of the exile of King Jehoiachin, and they sinned another six years until the exile of Zedekiah — that makes forty-six. And if you say that the years of Menasseh were fifty-five: Menasseh repented for thirty-three years, and all the years of his wickedness were twenty-two, as they said in the aggadah of חֵלֶק, and those of Amon two, and eleven for Jehoiakim, and corresponding to them for Zedekiah. Go and compute for four hundred and thirty-six years the shemittot and jubilees within them, and they are sixteen per hundred — fourteen shemittot and two jubilees. So for four hundred years: sixty-four; for thirty-six years: five shemittot — that makes seventy less one, and one extra year that enters into the completing shemittah to make seventy. And upon them was decreed seventy full years, as it says in Chronicles (II Chronicles 36): ״עַד רָצְתָה הָאָרֶץ אֶת שַׁבְּתוֹתֶיהָ … לְמַלֹּאות שִׁבְעִים שָׁנָה״ (Seder Olam)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {1 "The phrase וְאִ\"תֹּ (if you say) introduces an alternative reckoning of Menasseh's years of wickedness; the arithmetic resolves the apparent shortfall to reach exactly seventy shemittah-years against the seventy of exile."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:08:53.750082884Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}